<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria Hebrosbank has 2.02 mln lev profit for 96.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria Hebrosbank has 2.02 mln lev profit for 96.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's state-owned Hebrosbank posted 2.02 million lev net profit for 1996, the bank's balance sheet published in the State Gazette showed.</p>
<p>Comparative figures for 1995 were not available.</p>
<p>Figures from the bank's balance sheet and profit and loss account follow in million levs unless stated otherwise:</p>
<p>							    1996</p>
<p> Total revenue				     276,260.073</p>
<p> Net income on financial operations	   43,737.102</p>
<p> Net extraordinary				   7,044.583</p>
<p> Business and administration costs	     2,207.628</p>
<p> Provisions					   48,490.537</p>
<p> Taxes						     113.630</p>
<p> Profit							2.022</p>
<p> Uncompensated losses for previous years	  255.242</p>
<p> Total assets					119,294.157</p>
<p> Cash						    8,609.361</p>
<p> Treasury portfolio				 60,703.120</p>
<p> Extended interbank deposits		    12,109.846</p>
<p> Attracted interbank deposits		    8,633.980</p>
<p>Attracted deposits from</p>
<p> non-financial clients			    49,694.756</p>
<p> Lending to non-financial clients	     35,840.643</p>
<p> Non-financial assets				1,321.908</p>
<p> Equity capital				     10,538.296</p>
<p> Reserves, including provisions		 49,347.726</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 911 88</p>
<p>($ = 1575 Bulgarian Levs)</p>
</text>
